Are you an experienced Account Manager with a strong understanding of the German market? We are looking for a German-speaking Key Account Manager to manage and further develop their most important B2B accounts in Germany. You’ll have your own portfolio, significant commercial responsibility and the freedom to determine how you grow your accounts.
- Manage and grow a portfolio of key German B2B accounts;
- Develop account plans with clear revenue and growth targets;
- Negotiate annual agreements, pricing and commercial terms while protecting margins;
- Build strong relationships with purchasing, category management and decision-makers;
- Identify cross-selling and upselling opportunities;
- Introduce new products and product lines to your accounts;
- Identify and acquire new clients with key-account potential;
- Regularly visit clients and attend trade fairs in Germany;
- Translate market and customer insights into commercial opportunities;
- Work closely with sales support, purchasing and logistics.

You’ll also act as an important link between the German market and the internal commercial team, providing insights that can influence product range, pricing and the German B2B webshop.RequirementsWho are you?- Fluent in German, including professional-level negotiation skills;
- Good command of English and/or Dutch;
- At least 5 years of experience in Account Management or Key Account Management;
- Experience in B2B, distribution, retail or e-commerce is preferred;
- Strong negotiation and relationship-management skills;
- Commercially driven and focused on long-term account development;
- Able to work independently and take ownership of your targets;
- Willing to travel regularly to Germany for client visits and trade fairs;
- A relevant network within the German reseller or retail market is a plus.

Benefits- Performance-based bonus of up to 50% of the monthly salary;
- 26 vacation days with the option to purchase 5 additional days;
- 8% holiday allowance;
- Full

What will you be doing?
As a Production Employee, you play an important role in the preparation and packaging of food products. Together with your team, you help keep production running efficiently while making sure quality and safety standards are met. Your attention to detail and proactive attitude contribute to a smooth workflow and a well-organized production environment.

Your responsibilities include:

• Packing and preparing finished products so they are ready for shipment;
• Setting up, operating, and monitoring production equipment during the manufacturing process;
• Performing quality checks on products, packaging, and labeling to ensure all requirements are met;
• Keeping the work area clean, tidy, and compliant with hygiene and safety regulations;
• Collaborating with colleagues and supervisors to achieve production goals and meet daily schedules.

Functie-eisen:
What are we looking for?

• You have a good command of either English, Dutch, or both, allowing you to understand procedures and work safely within a production environment;
• You enjoy working in different locations and are open to being assigned to various production facilities throughout the region;
• You are flexible regarding working hours and can work rotating shifts, including mornings, afternoons, evenings, and nights for 16 to 32 hours per week;
• You are eager to learn new skills, adapt quickly to changing tasks, and become familiar with different production equipment;
• You have an eye for detail, value quality, and actively contribute to a clean, organized, and safe workplace.

As a Warehouse Employee at Dynalogic, you will work in a team of approximately 10 to 15 colleagues, ensuring that parcels are processed safely and efficiently. Your responsibilities include:
• Sorting and checking parcels;
• Loading and unloading trucks;
• Moving goods using an electric pallet truck;
• Scanning products manually;
• Picking and preparing orders for shipment;
• Processing and storing returned goods;
• Moving orders to the correct loading dock;
• Maintaining a safe, clean and organised workplace.
Come and meet us during our recruitment day
You're welcome to visit Dynalogic in Bleiswijk on Wednesday, October 21, between 11:00 AM and 2:00 PM. Simply register using the form on this page.

Functie-eisen:
For the Warehouse Employee position, we are looking for someone who works accurately, enjoys hands-on tasks and performs well in a dynamic environment.
• You have a VMBO-level education or equivalent experience;
• You can work independently and remain accurate under pressure;
• You are willing to work in a 5-shift system;
• You speak Dutch or English;
• You live within 20 kilometres of the warehouse;
• You have your own transport;
• A valid forklift, reach truck or clamp truck certificate is a plus, but not required!
Don't meet all the requirements or interested in other positions? You're still more than welcome to join our recruitment day.

Wat je gaat doen As a production worker in the cheese factory, you work in the shaving department. Here, large cheese blocks are prepared for the next stage of production.

Your tasks include:- placing 15 kg cheese blocks at your workstation;
- using a machine to remove the outer layer of the cheese;
- checking that the cheese is processed correctly;
- moving processed cheese with an electric pallet truck;
- keeping your workstation clean, safe and organised;
- working with your team to achieve the daily production targets.

Do you not yet have experience with an EPT? That is not a problem. You can learn this on the job and may have the opportunity to obtain your EPT certificate.   Wat we je bieden Your work as a production worker is rewarded with:
- a base salary of €18,16 gross per hour;
- a 30% allowance between 18:00 and 22:00;
- a 40% allowance between 22:00 and 07:00;
- a performance bonus of up to €2.00 gross per hour;
- a full-time job in a stable 3-shift schedule;
- free weekends;
- 8% holiday pay;
- 20 vacation days and 4 additional days in a flex budget;
- travel allowance from 10 km;
- the prospect of a permanent contract;
- on-the-job training and the opportunity to obtain an EPT certificate;
- personal support from Start People at the production location.

At Start People, we operate on the principle of equal pay; your terms and conditions of employment always match those of colleagues who are employed directly by the client. This means that, in addition to your hourly rate, your terms and conditions of employment also include, for example, the number of days off, allowances, time-off-in-lieu payments and other pay components.
   Functie-eisen This job is a good match if you:- can repeatedly lift cheese blocks weighing 15 kg;
- are comfortable with standing and physical work;
- are available full-time for morning, afternoon and night shifts;
- speak and understand Dutch or English;
- have your own reliable transport;
- already have your own accom
